# Photoreal CAD Instrument Render Bar

**STANDING DIRECTIVE (Tristan 2026-07-13):** Blender heroes, cutaways, and engineering drawing views must look **as photorealistic as possible from realistic CAD geometry**. They must **never** be LLM-generated images (no Gemini/i2i “polish”, no generative fill of product shots). Every choice goes in that direction. Fully **universal**. **Form follows function** (and hand/eye).

## The bar (pass/fail)

Ask of every shaded image and every plan/drawing that shows the product:

> Could a chartered engineer believe this is a Cycles render of real parametric CAD parts — not an AI picture and not a box of Lego?

| Must be TRUE | Must be FALSE |
|---|---|
| Geometry from CadQuery / forge-truth CAD families / honest engineering primitives | Cuboid proxies for recognisable parts (LED, TO-can, coin cell, cuvette, PCB) |
| PBR materials match role (FR4, metal can, glass IOR, matte polymer) | Flat clay grey on everything |
| Softbox / product studio for instruments; plant sky for plants | Fake “beauty” from an image model |
| Features forced by use-physics + HIG + beauty grammar | Named-product silhouette paste (Open Colorimeter as paste target) |
| Universal `isInstrumentDevice` (and class-agnostic plant paths) | Per-product branches |

Gold open-photometer photos remain the **TRAINING check** for whether the rules produce a real-looking object — never a texture or mesh to copy.

## Decision tree (every change)

1. Does this make the **CAD→Cycles** path more photoreal? → do it.
2. Does this add or rely on an **LLM image** of the product? → reject.
3. Is the shape forced by **function / hand / eye / manufacturing**? → keep.
4. Is it universal (`isInstrumentDevice` or geometry-family keyed)? → keep; else reject.

## Geometry sources (priority order)

1. **forge-truth CAD family STL** via `_import_family_cad` (seeded CadQuery)
2. **Compound engineering primitives** (cyl + dome LED, TO-can, hollow cuvette, coin-cell disk, ribbon pipe)
3. **Plain box** only for true planar parts (bench plate, baffle sheet, glass pane) — never for named components

Seed / extend families in `scripts/ingest/seed_internal_cad_assets.py` + CadQuery builders under `tier 1 and 2 parts for cad /`. proveCatch: `interior_authenticity_ok`.

## Materials (photoreal, not clay)

When a CAD mesh is imported, assign a **role material**, do not leave default grey:

| Role | Material language |
|---|---|
| PCB | FR4 green, slight roughness, packages darker |
| Coin cell | Brushed metal disk |
| Cuvette | Glass / clear polymer — low roughness, alpha, IOR |
| LED | Emissive body + clear dome |
| Photodiode | Dark metal TO-can + glass window |
| Enclosure | Charcoal matte polymer (see beauty grammar) |

## Forbidden

- LLM image generators as the hero / exterior / cutaway / drawing product image
- “Looks better in Midjourney/Gemini” as acceptance
- Cuboid LED / cuboid battery / solid-block cuvette / flat green slab as PCB when a family or compound exists
- Product-named special cases that bypass form-follows-function

